{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "def sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function sorts elements at indices divisible by three in a list,\n    while keeping other elements in their original positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = list(l)\n    elements_to_sort = []\n\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            elements_to_sort.append(l[i])\n\n    elements_to_sort.sort()\n\n    sorted_elements_iter = iter(elements_to_sort)\n    for i in range(len(result_list)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            result_list[i] = next(sorted_elements_iter)\n\n    return result_list"}
